WEBVTT

00:00.960 --> 00:02.080
Matthew 14

00:02.080 --> 00:08.620
At that time Herod the Tetrarch heard about the fame of Jesus, and he said to his servants,

00:09.460 --> 00:17.680
This is John the Baptist. He has been raised from the dead. That is why these miraculous powers are at work in him.

00:18.320 --> 00:24.500
For Herod had seized John and bound him and put him in prison for the sake of Herodias, his brother Philip's wife,

00:24.840 --> 00:27.040
because John had been saying to him,

00:27.040 --> 00:29.800
It is not lawful for you to have her.

00:31.320 --> 00:36.360
And though he wanted to put him to death, he feared the people because they held him to be a prophet.

00:37.140 --> 00:42.740
But when Herod's birthday came, the daughter of Herodias danced before the company and pleased Herod,

00:43.040 --> 00:47.760
so that he promised with an oath to give her whatever she might ask.

00:48.260 --> 00:49.820
Prompted by her mother, she said,

00:50.260 --> 00:54.420
Give me the head of John the Baptist here on a platter.

00:55.100 --> 00:56.860
And the king was sorry.

00:57.280 --> 01:01.580
But because of his oaths and his guests, he commanded it to be given.

01:02.180 --> 01:04.940
He sent and had John beheaded in the prison.

01:05.420 --> 01:10.060
And his head was brought on a platter and given to the girl, and she brought it to her mother.

01:10.580 --> 01:14.080
And his disciples came and took the body and buried it.

01:14.540 --> 01:16.380
And they went and told Jesus.

01:17.300 --> 01:22.640
Now when Jesus heard this, he withdrew from there in a boat to a desolate place by himself.

01:23.260 --> 01:26.700
But when the crowds heard it, they followed him on foot from the towns.

01:27.580 --> 01:33.240
When he went ashore, he saw a great crowd, and he had compassion on them and healed their sick.

01:34.040 --> 01:37.160
Now when it was evening, the disciples came to him and said,

01:37.940 --> 01:40.400
This is a desolate place, and the day is now over.

01:40.740 --> 01:44.200
Send the crowds away to go into the villages and buy food for themselves.

01:44.700 --> 01:45.980
But Jesus said,

01:46.860 --> 01:50.240
They need not go away. You give them something to eat.

01:51.000 --> 01:51.860
They said to him,

01:52.520 --> 01:55.460
We have only five loaves here and two fish.

01:56.280 --> 01:57.000
And he said,

01:57.580 --> 01:58.800
Bring them here to me.

01:59.540 --> 02:04.920
Then he ordered the crowds to sit down on the grass, and taking the five loaves and the two fish,

02:05.580 --> 02:07.940
he looked up to heaven and said a blessing.

02:08.660 --> 02:13.280
Then he broke the loaves and gave them to the disciples, and the disciples gave them to the crowds.

02:13.800 --> 02:16.020
And they all ate and were satisfied.

02:16.020 --> 02:20.800
And they took up twelve baskets full of the broken pieces left over.

02:21.580 --> 02:26.360
And those who ate were about five thousand men, besides women and children.

02:27.040 --> 02:28.040
And they all ate and were satisfied.

02:28.040 --> 02:34.540
Immediately he made the disciples get into the boat and go before him to the other side while he dismissed the crowds.

02:35.100 --> 02:39.520
And after he had dismissed the crowds, he went up on the mountain by himself to pray.

02:40.160 --> 02:42.600
When evening came, he was there alone.

02:43.020 --> 02:49.500
But the boat by this time was a long way from the land, beaten by the waves, for the wind was against them.

02:50.160 --> 02:55.040
And in the fourth watch of the night, he came to them walking on the sea.

02:55.680 --> 02:57.020
But when the disciples saw him, he said,

02:57.020 --> 02:59.900
When they saw him walking on the sea, they were terrified and said,

03:00.660 --> 03:02.020
It is a ghost.

03:02.680 --> 03:06.400
And they cried out in fear, but immediately Jesus spoke to them, saying,

03:07.200 --> 03:11.300
Take heart, it is I. Do not be afraid.

03:12.160 --> 03:13.360
And Peter answered him,

03:14.060 --> 03:19.740
Lord, if it is you, command me to come to you on the water.

03:20.520 --> 03:22.440
He said, Come.

03:23.060 --> 03:26.760
So Peter got out of the boat and walked on the water.

03:27.020 --> 03:28.060
And came to Jesus.

03:28.600 --> 03:33.040
But when he saw the wind, he was afraid, and beginning to sink, he cried out,

03:33.800 --> 03:36.300
Lord, save me.

03:37.240 --> 03:41.220
Jesus immediately reached out his hand and took hold of him, saying to him,

03:41.920 --> 03:44.680
O you of little faith, why did you doubt?

03:45.500 --> 03:51.920
And when they got into the boat, the wind ceased, and those in the boat worshipped him, saying,

03:52.440 --> 03:55.080
Truly you are the Son of God.

03:55.460 --> 03:57.000
And when they had crossed over,

03:57.020 --> 03:58.600
they came to land at Gennesaret.

03:59.080 --> 04:01.220
And when the men of that place recognized him,

04:01.480 --> 04:05.680
they sent around to all that region and brought to him all who were sick,

04:06.040 --> 04:09.420
and implored him that they might only touch the fringe of his garment.

04:10.000 --> 04:12.240
And as many as touched it were made well.

